IDE probe: don't require BSY during software reset.

The IDE driver asserts SRST, waits 1 ms, then checks that BSY came up to
decide a drive is present. QEMU finishes the reset from a bottom half well
inside that 1 ms, so BSY reads clear and every drive is called Not Present.
Drop the BSY check -- the reset itself still runs. Build-tree only, never
src/obp.

--- a/obp/dev/ide/ide.fth	2026-08-29 22:56:08.486983760 +0200
+++ b/obp/dev/ide/ide.fth	2026-08-29 22:56:08.500983823 +0200
@@ -278,6 +278,6 @@
 : (reset) ( check? -- ok? )
    6 2 ctrl!
    1 ms
-   if  1 wait-busy?  else  true  then
+   drop true
    2 2 ctrl!
 ;
